# Multi-select: Shift-click (or Cmd/Ctrl-click) adds and removes parts in the viewport and in Station Lanes.
# A drive script cannot hold keys, so the whole run holds Shift (BOWSHOCK_DRIVE_MODIFIERS); a plain click and Esc-to-clear are
# covered by the unit tests (app::multi). Run:
#   BOWSHOCK_DRIVE_MODIFIERS=shift cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/multiselect.drive out/multiselect
# Coordinates are for 1280x800 on the example rocket (viewport scene, lanes y 558..764; see lanes.drive).
viewport 1280x800
move (640, 400)
screenshot rest.png
# Shift-click the nose and the tube in the viewport: brackets on each, one `2 PARTS` tag, no handles; the Inspector shows only
# what they share (a mixed value as —), the status strip sums the mass.
click (441, 346)
click (588, 310)
screenshot viewport-two.png
# A third part joins.
click (770, 278)
screenshot viewport-three.png
# Clicking a selected part takes it out.
click (588, 310)
screenshot viewport-removed.png
# A click on empty space clears the selection (so does Esc: a headless run delivers no key events, the unit tests cover it).
click (600, 500)
screenshot cleared.png
# Station Lanes: Shift-click bars add too; every selected bar gets corner brackets.
click (408, 596)
click (571, 596)
click (922, 624)
screenshot lanes-three.png
click (922, 624)
screenshot lanes-two.png
